      "text": "TURING'S PHILOSOPHICAL MOVES:\n  1. Sidestep consciousness: the test focuses on behavior, not inner life.\n  2. The other-minds parallel: we infer thinking in other humans\n     from behavior too; why not apply the same standard to machines?\n  3. Objections anticipated: theological, mathematical, consciousness\n     objections -- Turing addresses each."
